			array( 'h' => 'Folding Cartons, Windows, and Simple Crayon Dividers', 'p' => array( 'A folding carton is efficient for standard crayon packs. A window box can show the colors directly. A tray-style carton can help larger sets stay organized. The divider should stop crayons from rubbing too much or falling into a pile during shipping.', 'Crayons are softer than pencils, so the box should avoid excessive pressure. The insert does not need artist-level grooves, but it should keep sticks aligned and easy for children to remove.' ) ),
			array( 'h' => 'Paperboard Choices for School Supply Pricing', 'p' => array( 'Duplex board and ivory paper are common because they support bright graphics at reasonable cost. Kraft paper can work for eco-learning products. The board should be strong enough for supermarket shelves and classroom handling without making the product too expensive.', 'See ' . vpn_batch_link( '/paper-materials-for-custom-paper-boxes/', 'paperboard materials for school product boxes' ) . ' when comparing paper thickness and print surface for school supply packaging.' ) ),
			array( 'h' => 'Safety Marks, Age Guidance, and Color Count Panels', 'p' => array( 'Eight details that define this product are crayon count, non-toxic mark, age range, wax stick diameter, classroom pack size, color naming, easy-open flap, and safety warning area. These are not the same details used for colored pencil packaging.', 'The front panel should show the color count clearly. The back panel can include safety claims, barcode, school supply information, recycling marks, and brand details. If the product is exported, reserve space for multilingual compliance text.' ) ),
